{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790281495,"nonce":"1+aIv0SnzJQAIpU1LbWp+jHmBSk=","title":"A string constant inside a constructor pattern never matched; abstracts' macros were never scanned or expanded","message":"`switch e { case W(\"5\"): }` and `e.match(W(\"5\"))` were always false: HirPattern::Literal compared a String literal to the scrutinee with a plain pointer `==`. Now haxe_string_compare. (Issue9403: `v.expr.match(EConst(CInt('9403')))`.)\n\nMacro functions inside an abstract were not registered, not stripped from runtime code (their bodies were compiled: \"unsupported expression type DollarIdent\" — Issue2640, 3753, 11212), and macro calls inside abstract method bodies were never expanded (expand_declaration skipped abstracts). Abstracts now scan, strip and expand like classes.\n\nRuntime `macro $v{literal}` builds the constant Expr.\n\nStill open: calling an INSTANCE macro (`a.test()`, receiver as the first argument) needs the receiver's type, i.e. lowering-time dispatch; Issue2640/3753/11212 now crash/compile-fail on that.","files":null}]}